cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark, please cite the software as follows."
title: "Systematic Benchmark of Visual Architectures, World Models and Exploration in Procgen"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Pedro Morato Lahoz"
repository-code: "https://github.com/PedroM2626/RL-Experiments-Lab"
license: MIT
version: "1.0"
date-released: "2026-09-23"
abstract: >-
  Five-seed, five-game, 100k-step comparison of visual feature extractors,
  world-model auxiliaries, augmentations, exploration bonuses and hierarchical
  controllers on Procgen, with RLiable aggregation (IQM, stratified bootstrap
  CIs, performance profiles, probability of improvement) and a JAX/Flax port of
  the same protocol.
keywords:
  - reinforcement-learning
  - procgen
  - benchmark
  - generalization
  - world-models
references:
  - type: conference-paper
    title: "Leveraging Averaged Structures and Regularized Sequence for Efficient Self-Supervised Visual Representation Learning"
  - type: conference-paper
    title: "Deep Reinforcement Learning at the Edge of the Statistical Precipice"
      authors:
        - name: "Rishabh Agarwal et al."
      year: 2021
      booktitle: "NeurIPS"
